timestamp=2026-09-26T20:00:42.866Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Close SSH hole; add anonymisation and deferred trusted-zone scripts\n\nFirewall:\n  Remove <service name=\\\"ssh\\\"/> from the public zone. sshd is disabled\n  and not listening, so the rule opened a door with nothing behind it.\n  firewalld merges this file over the built-in zone, so DHCPv6-client,\n  IPv6 NDP and PMTU/ICMP are unaffected.\n\n  Fix a latent XML bug: '--' is illegal inside XML comments, so the\n  file was never well-formed. firewalld's parser tolerated it, but any\n  stricter tool would have rejected the zone. Rewrote the comments and\n  documented why ICMP must stay unblocked (PMTU + IPv6 NDP).\n\nNew scripts:\n  set-anon-identity.sh       hostname -> zero on all interfaces, per-network\n                             random MAC, explicit DHCP hostname suppression\n  set-home-trusted-zone.sh  allow kdeconnectd only on a network you\n                             administer. Refuses open/WEP networks.\n                             DEFERRED - dry-run only, not applied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
