timestamp=2026-09-26T20:14:39.266Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat <<'EOF'\n  fail2ban.service contains:   PartOf=iptables.service firewalld.service ...\n  firewalld.service contains:  PartOf=dbus.service\n\n  PartOf= is BIDIRECTIONAL stop/restart propagation. So \"restart firewalld\"\n  transitively asks systemd to restart fail2ban -- while the same\n  transaction is already stopping it. systemd refuses: \"conflicting jobs\".\n\n  Arch's fail2ban unit should not have PartOf=firewalld.service. It only\n  needs After=firewalld.service, which it already has.\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
