timestamp=2026-09-26T20:18:04.956Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=external_directory pattern=/tmp/opencode/hss/* action.permission=external_directory action.pattern=/tmp/* action.action=allow
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:18:04.956Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add -A" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:18:04.956Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Replace broken public.xml override with validated workstation zone\n\nThe firewalld-workstation.conf approach was wrong on two counts and is\nremoved. A zone file cannot subtract an inherited service: <service>\naccepts only a name attribute, there is no remove-service element in\nfirewalld 2.5.2, and an /etc file sharing a built-in zone's name is\nMERGED rather than substituted. Overriding 'public' can therefore never\nproduce an empty allowlist.\n\nworkstation.xml is a uniquely-named zone, so it inherits nothing and\nstarts empty. Validated against firewalld 2.5.2's own zone_reader before\ninstalling. Result: all inbound denied except dhcpv6-client. ssh, mdns,\nsamba and kdeconnectd are all unreachable.\n\napply-firewall.sh installs and activates it, works around an Arch\npackaging bug (fail2ban.service declares PartOf=firewalld.service, which\npropagates restarts bidirectionally and makes 'systemctl restart\nfirewalld' fail with conflicting jobs), and refuses to report success\nunless nft rules are confirmed loaded. firewalld --state reports\n'running' even while enforcing nothing, so it is not a valid check.\n\nfail2ban-coverage.md documents that the sddm and sudo jails can never\nban anything: pam-generic requires an rhost=<IP> field, and both are\nlocal console events with no IP. unban-self.sh is the escape hatch for\nthe bantime=-1 self-lockout trap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
