timestamp=2026-09-26T20:22:33.210Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat >> ~/.config/fish/config.fish <<'EOF'\n\n# ── fail2ban readiness helper ───────────────────────────────────────────\n# fail2ban creates its control socket during Python init, so `systemctl\n# restart` returns (and reports \"active\") BEFORE the socket exists. Querying\n# immediately yields \"Failed to access socket path\". `ping` is also not a\n# sufficient gate: it answers once the server accepts connections, which is\n# before jails finish registering. Wait on the jail list instead.\nfunction f2bready\n    while not sudo fail2ban-client status 2>/dev/null | grep -q \"Jail list\"\n        sleep 0.5\n    end\n    sudo fail2ban-client status\nend\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
