timestamp=2026-09-26T20:26:52.321Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"fail2ban: drop dead jails, 24h bantime, pin zone to workstation\n\nThe sddm and sudo jails could never ban anything. pam-generic needs a\nliteral rhost=<IP> field to extract an address, and both are local\nconsole events with no IP: an SDDM greeter failure is someone at your\nkeyboard, a bad sudo password comes from a local tty. Removed rather\nthan left in place implying protection that does not exist. Real\ncoverage for those cases is pam_faillock deny=10 (sudo) and physical\nmeans (greeter). See fail2ban-coverage.md.\n\nbantime -1 -> 86400. A permanent ban is not self-cancelling; on a public\naddress a few wrong passwords would lock you out on every port with no\nexpiry. ignoreip covers RFC1918 but not tethering, cafe wifi, or\nairports, so the ban window is now finite.\n\nzone = workstation in [DEFAULT]. Without this the action inherits\nzone=public from /etc/fail2ban/action.d/firewallcmd-common.conf:37 and\nwrites every ban into a zone that is no longer bound to wlo1. Bans would\nbe reported successful while blocking nothing.\n\nAlso removed the superseded firewalld-workstation.conf, which could\nnever produce an empty allowlist and carried two schema defects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
