timestamp=2026-09-26T20:33:22.061Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Add bootstrap.sh; fix MAC randomization property name\n\nbootstrap.sh reapplies the whole verified baseline on a fresh install:\npackages, workstation firewall zone, fail2ban with the zone pin, and\nanonymisation. Idempotent, with a --check mode that changes nothing.\n\nEvery step verifies its own result and the script exits non-zero if the\nmachine does not end up in the expected state. The firewall check\nrequires loaded nft tables rather than trusting 'firewalld --state',\nwhich reports running even while enforcing nothing.\n\nIt also reproduces the two non-obvious workarounds this config depends on:\n  - fail2ban's PartOf=firewalld.service bug, which makes a plain\n    'systemctl restart firewalld' fail with conflicting jobs\n  - recidive's bootstrap, enabled only once /var/log/fail2ban.log exists\n    (a missing log aborts every jail at startup)\n\nset-anon-identity.sh used 802-11-wireless.mac-address-mode, which does\nnot exist in NetworkManager 1.58, so the MAC change silently failed and\nthe hardware MAC kept broadcasting. It now detects the available\nproperty (802-11-wireless.mac-address-randomization on NM >= 1.42) and\nfails loudly instead of reporting success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
