timestamp=2026-09-26T20:35:59.448Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add hardlock/bde-hardlock.pam hardlock/install-hardlock.sh pam/modules/bde-auth" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:35:59.448Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"hardlock: fail open when the biometric verifier is unavailable\n\nInstalling this on this machine would have locked out login, sudo and sshd.\n\ninstall-hardlock.sh appended two lines to every PAM stack it hooked:\n\n    auth [success=1 default=ignore] /usr/local/bin/bde-auth\n    auth required pam_deny.so\n\nbde-auth exited non-zero on ANY exception, so a daemon that was not running,\na missing socket or a timeout fell through to pam_deny.so and the correct\npassword still failed. It also hooked sshd, turning a local mistake into a\nremote lockout with no console.\n\n- bde-auth now separates 'denied' (exit 1, real mismatch) from 'unavailable'\n  (exit 2, no verdict) and honours BDE_FAILMODE, default 'open'\n- socket path resolves the target user via pwd, not os.getuid() -- PAM runs as\n  root, so getuid() is 0 and was the wrong answer\n- pam_deny.so removed from the stack so default=ignore returns to pam_unix\n- sshd excluded unless BDE_INCLUDE_SSHD=1\n- installer takes backups, supports --dry-run, and refuses to run without an\n  executable bde-auth\n- dropped the BlackArch-specific /usr/share/blackarch package step\n\nVerified: failmode=open exits 0 with no daemon, failmode=closed exits 1.\nInstaller --dry-run touches nothing. Not installed.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:35:59.448Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git log --oneline" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:35:59.448Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="head -3" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
