timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:28.197Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add faillock.conf deploy-faillock-admin.sh" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:28.197Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"faillock: add ordered deploy script, fix malformed audit/silent flags\n\nDeployment: deploy-faillock-admin.sh makes livings the only account\npam_faillock will never lock out. NOT DEPLOYED -- needs root.\n\nThe ordering is the substance. It backs up the config, creates shield-admin,\nenrols livings, then READS THE GROUP DATABASE BACK and only then installs a\nconfig naming admin_group. If the group is missing or the admin is not in it,\npam_faillock finds no exempt members and locks the admin out like everyone\nelse, so the script aborts before touching the config. It also writes\n/etc/shield-kitty/enroll.lock so no other account can enrol itself.\n\n--check reports state read-only; --revert restores the newest backup.\n\nTwo bugs fixed, both found by testing rather than reading:\n\n- 'audit = silent' -- audit and silent are BARE FLAGS in faillock.conf(5),\n  not key=value. As written it was one key carrying a meaningless value.\n  Now two separate flags, with silent kept because pam_faillock(8) warns\n  that preauth without it leaks whether an account exists.\n\n- group membership parsing. 'getent group' prints name:x:gid:mem1,mem2, so\n  the member list is field 4. The old one-liner split on ',' alone, leaving\n  'name:x:gid:' glued to the first member so grep -x never matched. The\n  verification would have passed unconditionally -- or failed, depending on\n  which direction it was read. Fixed with cut -d: -f4 in both the script and\n  the instructions in faillock.conf.\n\nVerified the step-4 predicate against six states: it proceeds only when\nlivings is genuinely a member AND the config names the group, and aborts\nwhen the group is absent, empty, holds a different member, or the config\nis missing. unlock_time stays 30s -- permanent lockout (unlock_time=0) is\ndeliberately not enabled, since with a broken exemption it is unrecoverable.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:28.198Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git log --oneline" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:28.198Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="head -2" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
