timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:33.830Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"faillock admin exemption PREPARED, NOT deployed (needs sudo). deploy-faillock-admin.sh orders it safely: backup -> create shield-admin -> enrol livings -> READ GROUP DB BACK -> only then install config naming admin_group, then write enroll.lock. Aborts if livings is not verifiably a member, because pam_faillock would otherwise lock the admin out like everyone else. Run: sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/deploy-faillock-admin.sh --check | deploy | --revert\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:33.831Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="tail -1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:33.831Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"faillock: fixed 'audit = silent' (audit/silent are BARE FLAGS not key=value) and fixed group parsing that split on ',' instead of cutting field 4 from 'name:x:gid:mem1,mem2' -- old check passed unconditionally. unlock_time stays 30s, permanent lockout (0) NOT enabled: no other login users exist on this box anyway, and it is unrecoverable if the exemption breaks\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:45:33.831Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog warn \"3 pam_faillock facts confirmed from man pages: (1) unlock_time=0 = never, needs faillock(8) --reset; (2) default dir /var/run/faillock is tmpfs so tallies+any permanent lock VANISH on reboot -- real permanence needs dir= off tmpfs; (3) admin_group members are treated like root, so even_deny_root would defeat the exemption. Live /etc/security/faillock.conf had no admin_group at all, so livings was lockable\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
