timestamp=2026-09-26T20:50:09.834Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"docs: correct stale permanent-ban claims to the actual 86400\n\nunban-self.sh and fail2ban-coverage.md both claimed the policy was\n'bantime = -1 (permanent)'. It is not: the live /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/\nshield-kitty.conf and the repo config both specify bantime = 86400 (24h) on\nthe sshd and recidive jails.\n\nThis mattered in the worst possible direction. unban-self.sh is the emergency\nescape hatch, and its own header described a failure mode that does not exist\nwhile omitting the real one: a ban expires after a day on its own, so the\ncorrect recovery advice is 'wait', not 'run this as root'. Also refreshed a\nstale address (10.245.106.176 -> 10.197.250.246).\n\nNo config change. The 1-day lockout the user asked for was already live.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
