timestamp=2026-09-26T20:53:36.950Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"fail2ban: recidive enabled=true in repo, matching live by request\n\nThe live /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/shield-kitty.conf had 'enabled = true' for the\nrecidive jail while the repo said false. That was not drift to revert -- the\nuser confirmed enabling it deliberately. The repo now records the real steady\nstate, and the two are byte-identical on every functional line.\n\nKept the bootstrap-order warning, because it is still true for a NEW machine:\nrecidive reads /var/log/fail2ban.log, and where fail2ban has never run that\nfile is absent, which aborts the whole startup and takes every other jail\ndown with it. The comment now separates 'done here on 2026-09-26' from 'still\nrequired on a fresh deploy'.\n\nVerified the preconditions that make enabling it safe, rather than trusting\nthat it was already running:\n  /var/log/fail2ban.log  present, root:root 0600, 34K\n  loglevel               INFO in fail2ban.conf -- below WARNING, recidive\n                         never observes the Ban events it exists to count\n  backend + logpath      polling + that file; the journal has no such log\n  fail2ban-client -t     OK: configuration test is successful\n\nAll three jails (DEFAULT, sshd, recidive) are bantime = 86400.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
