timestamp=2026-09-26T20:59:34.594Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add arpwatch-spoof-alert.sh arpwatch-spoof.service install-arpwatch-spoof.sh" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T20:59:34.594Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"security: add ARP spoof detection via arpwatch, notifying via Shield Kitty\n\nCloses the one real gap left in local hardening. Nothing on this machine could\ndetect system spoofing: no arpwatch, no suricata, no zeek, no tcpdump, no\ntpm2-tools, and no spoofing logic in any repo. fail2ban structurally cannot do\nthis -- it parses auth logs for repeated failures and has no notion of ARP,\nDHCP, hostname or MAC spoofing. arpwatch is in the extra repo (3.9-1).\n\narpwatch-spoof-alert.sh is the exec hook. It alerts on ONE event: a flip-flop,\na single IP claiming two different MACs. New hosts and departures are routine\nwith DHCP and are logged, never alerted. Own IP and gateway are skipped.\n\nNO AUTO-BAN, deliberately. The 1-day ban stays with fail2ban, which keys on\nreal connection and auth attempts. On this network a flipped MAC is usually\nAndroid or Windows per-SSID MAC randomisation, and the machine sits on a /8\nwith 16.7M addresses of other people on it -- a 24h ban on a flip-flop would\ncut off colleagues and randomising phones, not attackers. This notifies and\nlogs; a human decides.\n\nTwo bugs found by testing, both of which would have failed in production:\n\n- The alert payload was built as events:[\\\"str\\\", ...]. shield-kitty-alert.py\n  calls .get() on each element, so every spoof alert raised AttributeError and\n  was LOST. The schema is events:[{label,count,sample}]. The headline is\n  generated by the alert script, so passing one in was also wrong.\n- The unit ran the hook as root, and the log/db as root, while the installer\n  omitted sudo on the log. notify-send needs the USER session bus, so a\n  root-run hook delivers the alert to nobody. arpwatch now starts as root for\n  the AF_PACKET socket and drops to livings via -u, with both writable paths\n  owned by livings. The DB moved out of ~ so ProtectHome=read-only still holds.\n\nVerified: 7/7 on classification (flip-flop alerts, new host silent, own IP and\ngateway ignored, MAC case/dash normalisation, identical MAC not a flip,\nmalformed args exit 0), plus a live end-to-end delivery through the real\nnotify-send path -- no traceback, notification returned 0.\n\nNOT INSTALLED -- needs root:\n  sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh --dry-run\n  sudo ~/Projects/zen-hardening/install-arpwatch-spoof.sh\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
