timestamp=2026-09-26T21:02:01.282Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"fix: resolve paths via SUDO_USER, bootstrap session env for notify\n\nTwo bugs, both found by running the installer the way the user actually ran it.\n\n1. sudo resets HOME to /root, so HOOK=\\\"\\$HOME/Projects/...\\\" resolved to\n   /root/Projects/... and the installer aborted with 'hook not executable'.\n   Now resolves the real home from SUDO_USER via getent, and rewrites the\n   unit's hardcoded path plus an explicit Environment=HOME at install time.\n\n2. The worse one, and it would have been silent. The hook is a child of\n   arpwatch, which systemd starts as root and which drops privileges with -u.\n   -u changes the uid but NOT the environment, so the hook inherited neither\n   DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY nor DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS, and every spoof\n   notification failed. The log line was written; no notification appeared.\n   Same class of failure as the root-run-hook bug fixed in the previous\n   commit, one level further down.\n\n   The hook now reconstructs the session from the user bus socket\n   (/run/user/\\$UID/bus), and picks up a Wayland socket if present. Verified\n   directly: notify-send with only those vars exits 0, while notify-send with\n   a bare environment fails 'Cannot autolaunch D-Bus without X11 \\$DISPLAY'.\n\n   The alert script path is now derived from BASH_SOURCE rather than \\$HOME,\n   since it is a sibling directory of the hook's parent. That is independent\n   of who runs it, so it cannot break again the same way.\n\nAlso: the notifier's output is captured and routed through log() instead of\nbeing redirected into \\$LOG. When the log was not writable the redirect itself\nfailed and the actual delivery error was lost -- visible only when you most\nneeded to read it.\n\n7/7 classification tests still pass; installer dry-run verified under\n'env -i HOME=/root SUDO_USER=livings'.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:02:01.282Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git log --oneline" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:02:01.282Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="head -1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
