timestamp=2026-09-26T21:02:04.282Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"arpwatch installer aborted under sudo: 'hook not executable: /root/Projects/...'. sudo resets HOME to /root, so \\$HOME/Projects resolved into /root. Fixed by resolving the real home from SUDO_USER via getent and rewriting the unit path + Environment=HOME at install time. Also found a SECOND silent bug the same way: the hook is arpwatch's child, and arpwatch starts as root then drops privs with -u, which changes uid but NOT the environment -- so the hook had no DISPLAY/DBUS and every spoof notification failed while the log line still appeared. Fixed by reconstructing the session from /run/user/UID/bus. Verified: notify-send with only the bootstrapped vars exits 0, bare env fails 'Cannot autolaunch D-Bus'. commit b39490a\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
