timestamp=2026-09-26T21:15:15.400Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"arpwatch-spoof.service exited 1 in a restart loop: I used original-LBL-arpwatch flags, but the extra-repo 3.9 build has NO -a exec hook, no -u, no -c, and wants -i INTERFACE not positional. Rewrote detection to poll the datafile via arpwatch-spoof-scan.sh on a 2min timer, unit now uses -F -i wlo1 -f arp.dat -s -q -N -z (-N matters, this is a /8 so most traffic looks like a bogon). Found+fixed 3 bugs: comma-based MAC counting false-alarmed on same MAC with different case; stale state file swallowed a returning spoof; installer/scanner/unit disagreed on the datafile name. 12/12 tests pass incl. dedup lifecycle and 5000-row scale. commit 7dc7a07\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
