timestamp=2026-09-26T21:19:55.088Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Add reboot-persistence fixes found in the 2026-09-26 audit\n\nTwo defects that would have degraded the machine after the next reboot.\n\n1. Shield Kitty had no systemd unit installed anywhere. The watcher was\nrunning as a bare process, so it would simply have stopped existing once\nthe session ended. install-shield-kitty-units.sh installs the units and\nenables lingering so the user manager starts at boot without a login --\na security monitor that only runs when someone is logged in is not a\nmonitor.\n\n   The shipped units use %h in ExecStart, which in a system unit expands\n   to ROOT's home, giving /root/Projects/shield-kitty/... and a unit that\n   can never start. They are therefore installed as user units, which\n   also lets the alert path reach the user's display socket.\n\n2. bootstrap.sh only ever enabled recidive, never disabled it, and its\n   comment claimed the source shipped disabled. The source now ships\n   enabled=true to match this machine, so a fresh install would copy\n   enabled=true with no /var/log/fail2ban.log present, and a jail\n   pointing at a missing log aborts every fail2ban jail at startup.\n\n   The flag is now set in both directions to match reality, and scoped to\n   the [recidive] section with awk: 'enabled = true' appears under [sshd]\n   as well, so a blanket sed would silently disable the sshd jail.\n\nAlso adds install-audit-readonly.sh, which grants passwordless sudo over\nroot-owned wrappers rather than over nft/btrfs/firewall-cmd/fail2ban-client\ndirectly -- those binaries mutate state, so allowing them unpassworded\nwould be equivalent to root. The installer verifies each helper actually\nworks, not just that the sudoers file parses, after two attempts that\nparsed cleanly and did not work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
