timestamp=2026-09-26T21:22:13.340Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"fix: bound the arpwatch parse probe, which hung the install as root\n\nThe installer appeared to freeze on 'already installed'. It was not: my\nparse-check was running 'arpwatch <flags>' in the foreground, and under sudo\nthat succeeds, opens the raw socket, and never returns. -F is exactly what makes\narpwatch stay in the foreground, so the probe blocked on a perfectly healthy\narpwatch.\n\nWorse, the check had only ever been exercised unprivileged, where arpwatch\nfails on the socket and exits at once -- the one case that returns. Verified as\nroot: it hangs indefinitely.\n\nFixed by bounding the probe with 'timeout 3' and treating exit 124 as success,\nsince 'still running after 3s' is the positive signal that the flags parsed. The\nreal signal is the absence of a usage message, which distinguishes a rejected\nflag from a successful start under both root and unprivileged. The probe also\nwrites to a temp datafile so it cannot disturb the live one.\n\nTested all three paths: root-and-hanging, unprivileged-fast-exit, and\nbad-flag-prints-usage. The real binary agrees: no -q passes, with -q is\nrejected. Full dry-run now completes in 0.05s.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
