timestamp=2026-09-26T21:22:15.757Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"install-arpwatch-spoof.sh appeared frozen on 'already installed'. Cause: my new parse-check ran 'arpwatch ARGS' in the foreground; under sudo that succeeds, opens the raw socket and NEVER RETURNS (-F is what keeps it foreground). The check had only ever been tested unprivileged, where arpwatch fails on the socket and exits at once -- the single case that returns. Fixed with 'timeout 3', treating exit 124 as success ('still running' == flags parsed); the real signal is absence of a usage message, valid under both root and unprivileged. Probe now uses a temp datafile. All 3 paths tested. commit 54050ec\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
