timestamp=2026-09-26T21:31:18.661Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"arpwatch-spoof showed 'active (running)' but two real defects were hidden behind it. (1) arpwatch-spoof-scan.service had no User=, inherited root, and the scanner resolves XDG_RUNTIME_DIR from its own uid -> /run/user/0, a bus that does not exist, so notifications would fail SILENTLY while the scan looked healthy. Now User=livings + explicit XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/DBUS. (2) install-arpwatch-spoof.sh ran 'install /dev/null \\$DB' unconditionally, TRUNCATING arp.dat on every re-run, destroying collected addresses while the collector was appending to it -- that is also why the datafile looked absent. Now created only when missing. Also /var/lib/arpwatch was 0750 root:root, locking livings out of the dir regardless of file mode; now 0755 + spoof-state 0644 livings:livings so dedup can be rewritten. WorkingDirectory=/var/lib/arpwatch to fix arpwatch's /usr/arpwatch chdir fallback to /. commit fafed7f\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:31:18.661Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="tail -1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
