timestamp=2026-09-26T21:34:25.565Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add -A" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:34:25.565Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"fix: arp.dat is written every 15 min, so the 2-min scan was reading stale data\n\nThe datafile stayed at 0 entries while the service sat there 'active\n(running)'. Cause, from SIGNALS in arpwatch(8):\n\n    Normally arpwatch updates arp.dat once every 15 minutes. The SIGHUP\n    signal causes it to update immediately.\n\nSo a 2-minute scan timer re-read the same 15-minute-old file seven times over,\nand an empty datafile is indistinguishable from a healthy one in systemctl\nstatus -- which is exactly what hid it. The 101-byte arp.dat- alongside it is\narpwatch's in-progress database, not corruption.\n\nThe scan unit now SIGHUPs the collector before reading, so each tick forces a\nflush. Doing that requires CAP_KILL against a root process, so the scan unit is\nroot again -- but this time the session bus is pinned to the desktop user's\nruntime dir rather than derived from uid, which is what broke it last time.\n'Privileged' and 'which session do I notify' are now independent decisions.\n\nAdded -P /run/arpwatch-spoof.pid so the signal targets the exact process instead\nof a pidof match, and the installer probes with a throwaway pidfile.\n\nAlso added -D /var/lib/arpwatch. This build's compiled-in arpdir is\n/usr/arpwatch, which does not exist, so arpwatch logged a chdir warning and fell\nback to the working directory -- meaning it never found ethercodes.dat, which\nthe package installs in /var/lib/arpwatch. MAC vendor names were silently absent\nfrom every report. The chdir warning is now gone.\n\nThe installer probe and the three units both still verify.\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:34:25.565Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git log --oneline" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
