timestamp=2026-09-26T21:34:31.301Z level=INFO run=501861cf message="resolved path" arg=~/Projects/buildlog resolved=/home/livings/Projects/buildlog
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:34:31.302Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"arp.dat stayed at 0 entries while arpwatch-spoof showed 'active (running)'. Root cause from SIGNALS in arpwatch(8): 'arpwatch updates arp.dat once every 15 minutes. The SIGHUP signal causes it to update immediately.' So the 2-min scan timer re-read the same stale file 7x, and an empty datafile is indistinguishable from a healthy one in systemctl status. The 101-byte arp.dat- is arpwatch's in-progress DB, not corruption. Fix: scan unit now SIGHUPs the collector (needs CAP_KILL against root) before reading, via a new -P /run/arpwatch-spoof.pid rather than pidof. Scan unit is root again BUT the session bus is now pinned to /run/user/1000 explicitly instead of derived from uid, which is what silently broke notifications before. Also added -D /var/lib/arpwatch: this build's compiled-in arpdir /usr/arpwatch does not exist, so arpwatch never found ethercodes.dat (shipped in /var/lib/arpwatch) and MAC vendor names were silently missing from all reports. commit 706c458\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
