timestamp=2026-09-26T21:35:41.151Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add config/zen-hardening/fix-sudoers-permissions.sh config/zen-hardening/install-audit-readonly.sh" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:35:41.151Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Fix: stop quarantining the stock wheel sudo rule; validate sudoers per-file\n\nTwo bugs, the first of which broke sudo on the target machine.\n\n1. fix-sudoers-permissions.sh classified any 'ALL=(ALL) ALL' as\n   dangerous and quarantined it. That is the stock Arch rule\n   '%wheel ALL=(ALL) ALL' which grants wheel full sudo WITH a password\n   prompt. Removing it strips wheel of sudo entirely. Requiring a\n   password is the baseline, not a threat; only NOPASSWD removes the\n   password and only NOPASSWD warrants quarantine. Password-required\n   grants are now activated at 0440, and NOPASSWD is still quarantined.\n\n2. install-audit-readonly.sh gated on whole-tree 'visudo -c', which\n   exits non-zero when any unrelated file has bad permissions. It\n   therefore deleted its own valid drop-in while its own output showed\n   'parsed OK'. It now validates only its own file with 'visudo -cf',\n   and relies on the sudo -n probe as the real behavioural gate.\n\nAlso recorded: the session-created /etc/sudoers.d/opencode file was\nempty apart from its permissions, so it needed no quarantine at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
