timestamp=2026-09-26T21:42:11.197Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Add RECOVER-SUDO.sh: non-destructive sudo recovery\n\nRestores sudo after the sudoers lockout on 2026-09-26 without deleting\nor moving any sudoers file. Quarantine is removed as a concept, because\nthe outage happened when a script removed the only grant that let the\naccount run it.\n\nOrdering is the fix: restore the caller's own sudo access first, verify\nit behaviourally with an actual sudo call, and only then install the\naudit helpers. Previously two scripts each removed one of the two ways to\nrun the other, so the second failure cascaded into a lockout.\n\nResolves the invoking user from PKEXEC_UID. pkexec does not set\nSUDO_USER and USER is root under pkexec, so the first version audited\nroot and aborted with a misleading 'root is not in group wheel'. It\nfailed safe, before making changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
