timestamp=2026-09-26T21:43:44.178Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Fix audit-fail2ban jail list parsing\n\nfail2ban prints the jail list comma-separated ('recidive, sshd'). The\nwrapper split it on whitespace, producing a bogus jail named\n'recidive,' and reporting 'Sorry but the jail recidive, does not\nexist' -- which reads like a fail2ban fault rather than a wrapper bug.\nfail2ban itself was healthy throughout: 2 jails registered, sshd's\njournal filter correct.\n\nAlso note the confirmed end state from the completed audit: the\nfirewall's nft chain terminates in 'reject with icmpx\nadmin-prohibited', proving the default-deny actually holds and that\nkdeconnectd:1716 and mDNS:5353 are blocked despite being bound;\nbtrfs scrub reports no errors with all device error counters at zero;\nand the kernel log holds only benign probe messages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
