timestamp=2026-09-26T21:48:47.390Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="buildlog fix \"audit pass over the arpwatch work, 4 real defects. CRITICAL: scanner treated arp.dat as current state, but arpwatch only ADDS a row per mac/ip pair and never removes one, so one routine DHCP reassignment (laptop A yesterday, laptop B today, same IP) read as a permanent 2-MAC spoof that alerted once then said 'persists' forever -- guaranteed false positives on a /8 with lease churn. Fixed with a 1h window over the timestamp field arpwatch already writes; documented trade-off that a continuing spoof ages out after the window since the datafile cannot distinguish 'still spoofing' from 'seen once'. Also: ignored addresses were written to the state file, so un-ignoring one later made it match 'persists' and never alert. Installer: two mktemp -u calls left only one dir cleaned, orphaning a dir per root install; now one mktemp -d. Installer: units hardcoded /run/user/1000 while the installer resolved SUDO_USER for the home path; both now derived. 16/16 tests incl. both previously-broken cases; all scripts parse, all 3 units verify, no temp leak, notify path confirmed live. commit 3efc51f\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
