timestamp=2026-09-26T21:51:58.772Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git add -A config/zen-hardening/" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-09-26T21:51:58.772Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Fix the invoking-user resolution bug across all four root scripts\n\nThis is the same defect class that locked the account out of sudo, and\nit was still live in three of the four scripts that run as root.\n\nUnder pkexec, SUDO_USER is unset and USER=root. A script that reads\nSUDO_USER or \\$HOME therefore resolves to root and writes files for\nroot's account. install-arpwatch-spoof.sh was the worst case: it\ninstalled system units pointing at /run/user/0 and /root/Projects/...,\nwhich stay broken on disk permanently. install-shield-kitty-units.sh\ncould not find its unit sources. install-audit-readonly.sh and\nRECOVER-SUDO.sh both fell back to a hardcoded 'livings', which works\non this machine only by coincidence.\n\nRECOVER-SUDO.sh carried the bug inside the fix for it: its last-resort\nbranch was \\${USER:-livings}, i.e. root under pkexec. It only ever\nworked because PKEXEC_UID happened to be set.\n\nAll four now resolve in the same order -- PKEXEC_UID, then SUDO_USER,\nthen logname -- and treat 'root' as an unresolved value rather than a\nvalid answer, so a recovery script can never target root.\n\nAlso replaced '|| echo 1000' in the uid lookup, which would have\nquietly pointed units at another user's runtime dir, and restored\nDEST= in install-shield-kitty-units.sh after an edit of mine dropped\na definition that 7 lines depend on.\n\nVerified by extracting the real resolution block and executing it\nunder sudo, pkexec, a bare root shell, and PKEXEC_UID=0. All four\nreturn livings; the last returned root before this change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\" 2>&1" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
