timestamp=2026-09-26T21:55:41.772Z level=INFO run=01b4c3ae message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git -c user.name=opencode -c user.email=opencode@localhost commit -q -m \"Add git-verified.sh: make a false success structurally impossible\n\n'git push ... | sed && echo ok' printed ok after a push that failed\nwith exit 128, because the pipeline status is sed's. That is the same\ndefect class as the rest of the verification list, and the worst\ninstance of it: the others mis-set a value, this one asserts something\nthat is not true, which is how a failed backup gets reported as done.\n\ngit-verified.sh runs git without a pipe, propagates the real exit\nstatus, and says so on stderr. Verified: exit 0 on success, 128 on a\npush failure, 1 on a bad subcommand, so a failure cannot be chained\ninto a success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
