timestamp=2026-09-26T21:56:02.036Z level=INFO run=501861cf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="git commit -q -m \"log both alert outcomes, so silence is no longer ambiguous\n\nnotify-send is silent on success, and the previous code only logged when the\nnotifier produced output or exited non-zero. A successful send therefore wrote\nnothing at all, which made an empty log mean either 'delivered' or 'dropped'.\n\nThat ambiguity is the same one that hid the root-session-bus bug, where\nnotifications failed while every status check reported healthy. Four bugs this\nsession shared that shape; this removes the reason it was hard to spot.\n\nBoth the datafile scanner and the exec-hook test path now branch explicitly:\n\n    alert delivered ok for <ip>\n    alert DELIVERY FAILED for <ip> (rc=N): <output>\n\nVerified both branches with a stub notifier that exits 0 silently and one that\nexits 1 with output on stderr, plus the no-anomaly case which still logs\n'scan: no anomalies'. 16/16 of the existing suite still pass; the single failure\nin the combined run was my harness reusing scan.log across cases, confirmed by\nre-running it against a clean log (1 line, as expected).\"" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
